Drake and singer Keshia Chanté have shut down rumors that the Toronto rap superstar is the father of her unborn child.
According to a TMZ report, published on Wednesday (Oct. 7), a rep for singer Keshia Chanté released a statement denying rumors that Drizzy is the father of her unborn baby. However, the rep added that her unborn son&#x27;s father is a &quot;public figure in music.&quot;
Her statement comes after Drake&#x27;s PR team at The Agency Group told the media outlet on Tuesday (Oct. 6) that they completely and unequivocally deny the inaccurate paternity rumors .
Chanté announced her pregnancy to Hello! Canada on Oct. 6. Although she&#x27;s keeping the baby&#x27;s father&#x27;s identity private, the television personality shared that her partner was the one eager to begin building a family together.
&quot;I&#x27;m very free-spirited, and whatever the universe wants for me, I&#x27;ll have,&quot; she told the publication. &quot;But he said he was ready. He set up the play and he nailed it! God bless him.&quot;
Following Keshia Chanté&#x27;s pregnancy announcement, rumors surfaced on social media that Drake could be the pappy, which they both subsequently have denied. The 6 God and Chanté share a decades-long friendship that started when both were child stars in Canada. According to reports, Chanté was the muse for his 2018 viral hit &quot;In My Feelings&quot; ( &quot;Keke, do you love me?&quot; ). In 2022, during a performance at his OVO Fest, Drake brought the singer-actress out onstage and affectionately introduced her to the crowd as his &quot;first ever girlfriend.&quot; However, Keshia Chanté has always maintained that her relationship with Drake is strictly platonic.
